1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,747
Two brothers. Same salary. Same $5 a day.

2
00:00:04,017 --> 00:00:05,785
Max spends his on coffee.

3
00:00:05,855 --> 00:00:08,272
Leo invests his, every single day.

4
00:00:08,542 --> 00:00:11,830
$5 a day is $1,825 a year.

5
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:17,397
10 years later, Max has a pile of empty cups. Leo has $26,438.

6
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:19,482
20 years? $83,516.

7
00:00:19,702 --> 00:00:22,572
30 years? $206,742.

8
00:00:22,692 --> 00:00:26,967
Max spent $54,750 on coffee, and has nothing to show for it.

9
00:00:27,237 --> 00:00:31,315
That's compound interest. Your money earns money, and that money earns money too.

10
00:00:31,585 --> 00:00:33,770
You don't need more money. You need more years.

11
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:35,819
So… which brother are you?
